# Frontend Development Guidelines

## HTML Structure ([index.html](mdc:index.html))

### Best Practices
- **Semantic HTML**: Use proper tags for structure
- **Accessibility**: Include proper labels and ARIA attributes
- **Responsive Design**: Use viewport meta tag
- **Clean Structure**: Organize sections logically

### Key Components
```html
<!-- Header with clear title -->
<h1>🤖 Simple ChatGPT App</h1>

<!-- Input section with proper labeling -->
<div class="input-section">
    <label for="user-input">Ask ChatGPT anything:</label>
    <textarea id="user-input" placeholder="Type your question here..."></textarea>
</div>

<!-- Example questions for better UX -->
<div class="example-questions">
    <button class="example-btn" onclick="fillExample('text')">Example</button>
</div>

<!-- Response section with proper structure -->
<div class="response-section">
    <label>ChatGPT Response:</label>
    <div id="ai-response"></div>
</div>
```

## CSS Styling ([css/styles.css](mdc:css/styles.css))

### Design Principles
- **Modern Aesthetics**: Gradients, shadows, rounded corners
- **Responsive Layout**: Flexbox and media queries
- **Interactive States**: Hover, focus, disabled states
- **Consistent Spacing**: Use consistent padding/margins

### Key Styling Patterns
```css
/* Reset and base styles */
* {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    box-sizing: border-box;
}

/* Gradient backgrounds */
body {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%);
}

/* Modern card design */
.container {
    background: white;
    border-radius: 15px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 40px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
}

/* Interactive button states */
#send-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(102, 126, 234, 0.3);
}
```

### Color Scheme
- **Primary**: #667eea (Blue)
- **Secondary**: #764ba2 (Purple)
- **Text**: #333 (Dark gray)
- **Background**: #f8f9fa (Light gray)
- **Error**: #721c24 (Red)

## JavaScript Functionality ([js/api.js](mdc:js/api.js))

### API Integration Pattern
```javascript
async function sendToChatGPT() {
    // 1. Get user input
    const userInput = document.getElementById('user-input').value.trim();
    
    // 2. Validate input
    if (!userInput) {
        alert('Please enter a question first!');
        return;
    }
    
    // 3. Update UI for loading state
    sendBtn.disabled = true;
    sendBtn.textContent = 'Sending to ChatGPT...';
    
    try {
        // 4. Make API call
        const response = await fetch('http://localhost:8000/api/chat', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ message: userInput })
        });
        
        // 5. Handle response
        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP error! status: ${response.status}`);
        const data = await response.json();
        
        // 6. Display result
        displayResponse(data.response);
        
    } catch (error) {
        // 7. Handle errors gracefully
        console.error('❌ Error:', error);
        displayError(error.message);
    } finally {
        // 8. Reset UI state
        sendBtn.disabled = false;
        sendBtn.textContent = 'Send to ChatGPT';
    }
}
```

### Error Handling Best Practices
- **User-Friendly Messages**: Clear, actionable error text
- **Console Logging**: Detailed error information for debugging
- **Graceful Degradation**: UI remains functional even with errors
- **Loading States**: Visual feedback during async operations

### UI State Management
- **Loading States**: Disable buttons, show spinners
- **Error States**: Display error messages with styling
- **Success States**: Show results with proper formatting
- **Reset States**: Return to initial state after operations

## Development Workflow

### Making Changes
1. **HTML**: Edit structure, refresh browser
2. **CSS**: Modify styles, see immediate changes
3. **JavaScript**: Update logic, test functionality

### Testing
- **Manual Testing**: Use example buttons
- **Console Debugging**: Check browser console for errors
- **Network Inspection**: Monitor API calls in DevTools
- **Responsive Testing**: Test on different screen sizes

### Common Patterns
- **Event Listeners**: Use `addEventListener` for interactions
- **Async/Await**: Handle API calls properly
- **DOM Manipulation**: Update UI elements dynamically
- **Error Boundaries**: Catch and display errors gracefully

This guide ensures consistent, maintainable frontend development practices.
